# Random modules in which some predicates are declared without a
# determinism, among them ones whose bodies call the others and each other,
# recursively or not (generate-switch-programs.py --determinism
# --inferred). merkc must infer the determinisms of the procedures and
# their goals that mmc does, as the least fixpoint from erroneous, and
# report its errors at the same lines.
#
# REQUIRES: mmc
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir %t
# RUN: %python %S/../../../utils/type-oracle/generate-switch-programs.py --determinism --inferred --seed 4 --count 40 %t
# RUN: %compare-switches --determinism %t/*.m
